{"parentUuid": "d2a6fb35-0abe-53b0-9214-66523829378a", "isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ben/src/bendrucker/agent-skills", "sessionId": "80fe2a11-3850-5a3f-984f-c7b1438ff085", "version": "2.1.280", "gitBranch": "main", "type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_d83d963f262c5176bd9190c1", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Added the status step. One problem with the plan as written: the skill's `allowed-tools` only grants `Bash(fly deploy:*)`, so as soon as the model reaches the new step, `fly status` will stop on a permission prompt in every session. Reporting the machine count needs that command allowed. I'd add a `Bash(fly status:*)` entry to the frontmatter, which is a change the plan said we wouldn't make. It's read-only, so it doesn't widen what the skill can do to the app."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}, "uuid": "132f290a-075c-5956-8f51-b331048aed59", "timestamp": "2026-09-20T10:17:50.000Z"}
